    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Aga Khan University is part of the largest study on genetics of mental illness in Africa. The four-year project known as Neuropsychiatric Genetics of African Populations-Psychosis (NeuroGAP-Psychosis) seeks to engage 35,000 Africans in a quest to gain a deeper biological understanding of schizophrenia and bipolar disorder across a diversity of populations.",
